# Core Architecture Rules

## Domain-Driven Design (DDD)
- Each domain lives under `libs/{domain}/`
- Layer structure: `domain/` → `service/` → `datasource/`
- Cross-domain imports are forbidden (use shared interfaces)
- `libs/shared/` is the only cross-domain shared code

## Forbidden Patterns
- Direct cross-domain imports (e.g., `libs/order` importing from `libs/user`)
- Datasource imports from domain/service layers
- Circular dependencies between domains
